# Intent
Build a transparent Rewards shelf that makes the earned-points loop legible.
It supports a companion's level-up celebration only when a successful redeem
actually increases the returned level.

# Requirements
- Fetch `companion`, `items`, and `pointsBalance` from the UI data boundary.
- Disable unaffordable rewards and state how many points are missing.
- Render per-item redemption/loading/error states.
- Display accessory/theme/skip-token labels and companion mood without
  inventing functional reward effects.

# Interfaces
Use `RewardsResponse`, `Reward`, `Companion`, `getRewards`, `redeemReward`,
and `isFixtureMode` from `src/lib/ui-data.ts`.

# Output
`src/app/rewards/page.tsx`

# Acceptance criteria
- A redeem result updates balance and companion from the response.
- Level-up UI appears only when the returned level increases.
- A live API failure is labeled and never replaced with fixture data.
